.TH CLIDECOR 1 "2026" "1.0.0" "CLI DECOR Manual"
.SH NAME
clidecor \- blazing-fast, config-driven Neofetch replacement written in C++17
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clidecor
[\fIOPTION\fR] [\fIARGUMENT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
CLI DECOR displays system information (OS, kernel, CPU, memory, disk, etc.)
alongside custom image pixel art or ASCII logo art in your terminal.
It is designed to be sub-5ms, config-driven, and fully modular.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version number and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Launch the interactive TUI settings menu.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Fetch the latest source from GitHub, recompile, and reinstall in place.
Asks for confirmation before proceeding.
.TP
.B \-\-remove
Uninstall CLI DECOR, removing the binary, config directory, and shell aliases.
.TP
.B \-t \fI<theme>\fR
Set the active colour theme. Available themes:
\fBdefault\fR, \fBhacker\fR, \fBdracula\fR, \fBnord\fR, \fBfire\fR, \fBgold\fR, \fBchameleon\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-remind \fI"text"\fR
Set the reminder box text displayed at the bottom of the output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/clidecor/config.conf
Main configuration file. Edit to toggle modules, set themes, and configure image art.
.TP
.I ~/.config/clidecor/clidecor
The compiled binary installed by the installer.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Key configuration options (see config.conf for the full annotated list):
.PP
.nf
show_os=1           Show OS name
show_cpu=1          Show CPU + usage bar
show_memory=1       Show RAM usage bar
theme=default       Colour theme
image_path=         Path to custom PNG/JPG image
image_width=28      Image width in terminal columns
reminder_text=      Sticky reminder note shown on startup
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run normally:
.B clidecor
.TP
Open settings:
.B clidecor --settings
.TP
Switch to hacker theme:
.B clidecor -t hacker
.TP
Set a reminder:
.B clidecor --remind "Ship the code today"
.TP
Update to latest version:
.B clidecor --update
